<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fayzabad, Badakhshan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Faizabad (Afghanistan)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fayzabad is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, the capital of Badakhshan province, on the Kokcha river in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a>. From the 17th century it was the seat of the mirs who ruled Badakhshan, and it has long been the main market of the province, on routes towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamir-mountains">Pamirs</a>, Chitral and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fayzabad-badakhshan.jpg" alt="Fayzabad, Badakhshan" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian-G. Albert · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Feyzabad_in_Afghanistan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
